    A001["<div class='arg'><b>A001 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>The Fed's choice at the Sept FOMC is between a hike and risking a large bond spike.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Bond price action, including post Friday's CPI, shows the bond likes orthodoxy.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c scn'><span><b>ALT:</b> <b>SC001 - Fed holds: bond spike</b></span></div><div class='c scn'><span><b>ALT:</b> <b>SC002 - Hawkish presser after hike</b></span></div></div>"]
    A002["<div class='arg'><b>A002 · PREDICTION</b><div class='core pred'><span>The Fed hikes 25bp.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A001 - VIEW</b></span></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Friday's CPI data all but lock in a rate hike this week.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Chairman Warsh's Jackson Hole remarks, together with current market pricing, have raised the cost of disappointing expectations significantly.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Rate pricing is firmly in the zone to support a hike.</span><b>[A]</b></div></div>"]
    A003["<div class='arg'><b>A003 · PREDICTION</b><div class='core pred'><span>Warsh delivers a hawkish hike.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c pred'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A002 - PREDICTION</b></span></div><div class='c pred'><span><b>P:</b> Warsh in the presser is more Warsh as at Jackson Hole than Warsh as at the July FOMC.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Warsh's Jackson Hole-style presser is largely to support the bond.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c pred'><span><b>P:</b> Sept FOMC communications lean hawkish.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c scn'><span><b>ALT:</b> <b>SC003 - Warsh as at Jackson Hole</b></span></div><div class='c scn'><span><b>ALT:</b> <b>SC004 - Warsh not as at Jackson Hole</b></span></div></div>"]
    A004["<div class='arg'><b>A004 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>Warsh's hawkish hike supports higher front end rates and twist flattening of the UST curve.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c pred'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A003 - PREDICTION</b></span></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Warsh can point to Friday's twist flattening of the Treasury curve as evidence of tighter policy reinforcing inflation-fighting credibility.</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]
    A006["<div class='arg'><b>A006 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>With evolving expectations, considerable two-way risk remains for the USD at Wednesday's meeting.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c scn'><span><b>ALT:</b> <b>SC005 - Bullish USD case</b></span></div><div class='c scn'><span><b>ALT:</b> <b>SC006 - Bearish USD case: Fed holds</b></span></div></div>"]
    A005["<div class='arg'><b>A005 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>The USD outcome is determined by the Fed's ability to #quot;out-hawk#quot; market expectations and other G10 central banks.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A006 - VIEW</b></span></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> The bar for the FOMC to #quot;out-hawk#quot; both expectations as well as other G10 central banks is high.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> The high bar for the FOMC to #quot;out-hawk#quot; both expectations as well as other G10 central banks is partly the reason for the USD trading more-or-less sideways into year-end (ex-JPY).</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]
